    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12010" root="دبخ" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِبَارٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبَرِىٌّ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  You say
also, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٌ مَا يَدْرِى قِبَالَ الأَمْرِ مِنْ دِبَارِهِ</span> <i>Such a
one does not know the first part of the affair
from the last thereof.</i> (TA.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا يَعْرِفُ قِبَالًا</span>:
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْ دِبَارٍ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبِيرٌ</span>. And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَنْتَ لَهُمْ فِى قِبَالٍ وَلَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِبَارٍ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>Thou art not one for whom they care.</i>
(TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قبل</span>.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبْرٌ</span>: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُبَارٌ</span>.

